{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('draft/update13.json'))\nexp=d['experiment']\nexp['previous_id']='602b7dcab8064d2ab9113ac315a40743-experiment'\nexp['revision_reason']='Extended the probe past the re-queue: the harness now drives the re-queued proposal through the replica\\\\'s own handlePropose path, completes its fast-commit exchange, and then calls the target\\\\'s own execution entry point (Exec.executeCommand) so the client reply can be read from the proposal\\\\'s reply writer. The earlier scenario, ballots and crash points are unchanged.'\nexp['source_ids']=exp['source_ids']+['s-exec-reply']\nexp['anchors']=exp['anchors']+[{\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-exec-reply\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"strongconnect\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":124,\\\"end_line\\\":142}]\nexp['scope']['description']=exp['scope']['description']+' After the replacement decision and the observed re-queue, the harness calls handlePropose with the re-queued proposal (creating instance (0,1)), delivers that instance\\\\'s pre-accept replies, and invokes the package\\\\'s own execution entry point for it, recording the execution result, the reply writer size and the decoded reply.'\nexp['scope']['assumptions']=exp['scope']['assumptions']+['The execution entry point is invoked directly, as the package\\\\'s executeCommands goroutine would, because the harness runs no run() loop.']\nexp['scope']['parameters']=dict(exp['scope']['parameters'], reproposed_instance=1)\nexp['prefix']=exp['prefix']+' Then the re-queued proposal is passed to the replica\\\\'s own handlePropose, its pre-accept exchange is delivered, and Exec.executeCommand is called for instance (0,1); the reply written for command id 77 is decoded from the proposal\\\\'s reply writer.'\nexp['requirement']=exp['requirement']+' The re-queued proposal must also be able to complete: after it is decided, the target\\\\'s execution path must deliver a reply for the same command id.'\nexp['prerequisites']=exp['prerequisites']+[\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"client-request-requeued\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"client_request_requeued\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"command_id\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":77}]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"reproposed-instance-decided\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_reproposal_commit\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4}]}]\nexp['comparisons']=exp['comparisons']+[\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"completion_reply\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"client-request-requeued\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"command_id\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":77},\n  \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"After the re-queued request is decided again, the target's execution path produces a client reply carrying the same command id (77); violated when no reply is written or it carries a different command id.\\\"}]\nd['rationale']='Requested a fresh execution of the extended client-completion probe: the same scenario now continues past the re-queue, re-proposes the request through the target\\\\'s own propose path, and drives it through the target\\\\'s own execution entry point so the client reply is measured rather than assumed. A new source range covers the execution-time reply condition.'\nd['sources']=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-exec-reply\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"epa